<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Negara's reserves fell to 69.71 bln ringgit.</title>
<headline>Bank Negara's reserves fell to 69.71 bln ringgit.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Negara's gold, foreign exchange and other reserves fell to 69.71 billion ringgit as at May 31 against 71.12 billion a fortnight earlier, the Bank said in a statement on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The central bank said its total assets and liabilities dropped to 96.44 billion ringgit from 96.93 billion two weeks earlier.</p>
<p>(In bln ringgit)  May 31 1997     May 30 1996     May 15 1997</p>
<p>Reserves		 69.71	     66.74	     71.12</p>
<p>Assets		   96.44	     95.64	     96.93</p>
<p>Currency		 22.21	     19.67	     22.25</p>
<p>Govt paper		1.81		3.08		1.64</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
